---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const title = 'The Sellable-Numbers Scan guarantee | Decisive Finance';
const description =
  'At least 3x the Scan fee in owner-accepted value identified in 14 days, or you pay nothing. The exit-readiness guarantee mechanics, in full. Glass box.';

const resolutions = [
  {
    heading: 'The dollar path',
    body: 'At least 3x the Scan fee in quantified, owner-accepted value, named in writing by Day 14. Recoverable cash or margin, dollarized valuation exposure a buyer would price against you, or a diligence-killing finding caught while there is still time to fix it. This is the path most Scans hit.',
  },
  {
    heading: 'The strategic finding',
    body: 'If no dollar path exists at the required scale, a strategic finding of equivalent materiality confirmed in writing may substitute. A concentration risk that would cap the multiple, an owner-dependence problem that would gate the sale, or a pricing architecture change that materially resets the earnings.',
  },
  {
    heading: 'Full refund',
    body: 'If neither of the above is true at the Day 14 readout, you pay nothing. No argument, no conditions, no second look.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Guarantee</span>
      <h1>The Sellable-Numbers Scan guarantee.</h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        We run a 14-day Sellable-Numbers Scan for a fixed fee. By Day 14, one of three things is true, measured at the Day 14 readout, not on a later date: at least 3x the Scan fee in owner-accepted value identified, a strategic finding of equivalent materiality, or you pay nothing. We guarantee findings and dollarized exposure. We never guarantee a sale price or a multiple, because we do not control the market.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Three resolutions</span>
        <h2>Three ways the guarantee resolves.</h2>
        <ol class="engine-list">
          {resolutions.map((r) => (
            <li class="engine-item">
              <div>
                <strong>{r.heading}.</strong>
                <p>{r.body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Definition</span>
        <h2>What &ldquo;owner-accepted value&rdquo; means.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A sale price is a multiple times earnings, and the Scan works both numbers. Owner-accepted value is what the Scan surfaces, in dollars, on both sides of that equation, with a named path the owner signs off on. It falls into one of three categories:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Recoverable cash or margin: funds a decision can stop, redirect, or capture at current volume</li>
          <li>Valuation exposure: the dollars a buyer&rsquo;s diligence would knock off the number, named before the buyer names them</li>
          <li>Value expansion: pricing, mix, margin, and concentration upside a buyer would pay a multiple on</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="lede">
          Naming the number and the path is what the Scan is paid for. Capturing the number is what the 90-Day Resolution and the Exit-Value Partnership are paid for. The Scan guarantee measures the naming, not the capturing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Fit</span>
        <h2>Who the guarantee fits.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Owners of operating companies with $5M to $50M in revenue with an ownership change on the horizon in the next one to three years: a sale, a PE approach, a succession, a partner exit. You run on data and suspect your numbers would not survive the person writing the check.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          The floor is $5M in revenue. Below that, the guarantee math does not hold and we refer out. We do not sell companies, promise a sale price, or find you a buyer. We make the company worth believing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Credits and timing</span>
        <h2>How the Scan fee applies to what comes next.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A 90-Day Decision Resolution signed within 7 days of the Day 14 readout credits 100% of the Scan fee against the Resolution fee. Past Day 21, the Scan fee is sunk and no credit applies. The credit window rewards speed of decision, not urgency theater.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          Clients who continue to an Exit-Value Partnership pay a monthly retainer plus a 5% fee on confirmed Realized Value, validated quarterly against Financial Rhythms&#x2122; methodology, not opinion. No fee is ever calculated from the transaction or contingent on a closing. We are the one advisor in the deal who is not paid on the deal.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Pricing by revenue band</span>
        <h2>Fixed fees by company size.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          All engagements are fixed fee, banded by revenue, so the economics make sense at the company's scale before work begins.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          <strong>The Sellable-Numbers Scan</strong> (14 days): $10,000 for $5M to $8M revenue; $15,000 for $8M to $25M; $20,000 for $25M to $50M.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          <strong>The 90-Day Decision Resolution</strong>: $30,000 for $5M to $8M; $45,000 for $8M to $25M; $60,000 for $25M to $50M. Scan fee credits 100% if signed within 7 days of the Day 14 readout.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          <strong>The Exit-Value Partnership</strong> (monthly retainer, 12 to 24 months): $7,500 per month for $5M to $8M; $10,000 for $8M to $25M; $12,500 for $25M to $50M. Adds a 5% fee on quarterly-validated Realized Value. Fees tied to the value created, never to the deal.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Engagement letter</span>
        <h2>What is in the engagement letter.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Every term on this page is in the engagement letter, signed both sides before work begins. The guarantee is not stop-work. The owner keeps every deliverable produced through the Scan regardless of which of the three guarantee paths the engagement resolves to. The guarantee measures against the Day 14 readout, not a follow-up period.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          We don&rsquo;t audit the past. We make the company worth believing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2>Book 30 minutes with Russ.</h2>
        <p class="lede">No pitch. You leave knowing what a buyer would re-price.</p>
        <a href={CALENDLY} class="btn btn-primary">Book 30 minutes with Russ</a>
        <p class="closing-frame">Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
